<v Jim>It's just OK, huh? Cat got your tongue?
<v Jim>只是还行，嗯？被猫咬了舌头？

00:41:13.020 --> 00:41:44.810
<v Liz Weil>Later people, mostly men, sit around the hospitality suite. Jim pokes his head in. He grins and tells us that he's going upstairs with Marie. At 5:00 in the morning, Rod and Kate sheepishly come back from downtown. In the morning, the weekend ends with an egg and sausage breakfast, "Amazing Grace," and the SIA tradition of everybody hugging everybody else in the room.
<v Liz Weil>后来，人们，主要是男人，坐在招待套房里。吉姆探出头来。他笑着告诉我们他要和玛丽上楼。凌晨5点，罗德和凯特羞答答地从市中心回来。早上，周末在鸡蛋香肠早餐、“奇异恩典”和SIA拥抱房间里每个人的传统中结束。

00:41:44.810 --> 00:42:23.980
<v Liz Weil>Everybody looks exhausted, like students after exams. Martha spends a long time crying at the window, watching the cars pull out, talking about how she already misses the hugs. She's wearing her special hugs sweatshirt, the one with the poem sewn on the front. The loop appears to be starting over. Martha's returning to her empty trailer in Indiana, where she'll be lonely, and work evenings at Kmart, and save up her money for the next SIA event. But then something happens. A man pulls a game store coin out of his pocket. He gives it to her. She reads aloud.
<v Liz Weil>每个人看起来都筋疲力尽，就像考完试的学生。玛莎在窗前哭了很久，看着汽车驶离，说着她已经开始想念拥抱了。她穿着那件特别的拥抱运动衫，前面缝着那首诗。循环似乎要重新开始了。玛莎回到她印第安纳州空荡荡的拖车里，她会在那里感到孤独，在Kmart上夜班，并为下一次SIA活动存钱。但后来发生了一件事。一个男人从口袋里掏出一枚游戏店硬币。他给了她。她大声读出来。

00:42:23.980 --> 00:42:35.850
<v Martha>Good for a hug and a kiss anytime, anywhere. It doesn't say, any place. Can I have it?
