00:43:27.010 --> 00:44:08.950
<v Ira Glass>Act Three, Small town in the big city. The fact is a small town can be anywhere, even in the heart of what many people see as one of the harshest urban environments in the country. Paul Johnson, Carlos Appleby, and Sanantonio Brooks are teenagers living in public housing on Chicago's South Side at 4120 South Prairie. People who live there just call the building, 4120. It's a highrise building, 16 stories tall, 10 apartments on each floor, with an open air hallway on each floor that people who live there just call a porch. We sent them out with a tape recorder to their building to record what happens there, and then talked to them in our studios about how their building is like a small town.
<v Ira Glass>第三幕，大城市里的小镇。事实是，小镇可以在任何地方，甚至在许多人视为该国最严酷的城市环境之一的中心。保罗·约翰逊、卡洛斯·阿普尔比和萨南托尼奥·布鲁克斯是住在芝加哥南区普雷里南街4120号公共住房里的青少年。住在那里的人管这栋楼叫4120。这是一栋高层建筑，16层高，每层10间公寓，每层都有一个露天走廊，住在那里的人管它叫“门廊”。我们给他们一台录音机，让他们回到楼里记录那里发生的事情，然后在我们的工作室里和他们谈论他们的楼怎么像个小镇。

