<v Paul Johnson>是的，有地下室。

00:55:34.200 --> 00:55:35.820
<v Carlos Appleby>Yeah, and all that.
<v Carlos Appleby>是的，还有所有那些。

00:55:35.820 --> 00:55:38.910
<v Ira Glass>Why a basement, of all the things to name? Why a basement?
<v Ira Glass>为什么是地下室，在所有要命的名词里？为什么是地下室？

00:55:38.910 --> 00:55:43.150
<v Paul Johnson>You could throw a party down there, have card games.
<v Paul Johnson>你可以在那里开派对，打牌。

00:55:43.150 --> 00:56:20.110
<v Sanantonio Brooks>My auntie, she got a house with a basement in it, that's where she go when she don't want to be bothered with the people upstairs. She go downstairs in her basement. She got a nice little TV down there. There's some furniture down there. I'll always come back and visit the building, because that's where I grew up. It's fine there, but I wouldn't want to be there all my life.
<v Sanantonio Brooks>我姨妈，她有一栋带地下室的房子，那是当她不想被楼上的人打扰时去的地方。她下到地下室。她那儿有一台不错的小电视。那儿有些家具。我总是会回来看看这栋楼，因为那是我长大的地方。那里还行，但我不想一辈子都待在那里。

00:56:20.110 --> 00:56:45.570
<v Ira Glass>If their building is, in fact, a kind of small town, then when they move away, Sanantonio, and Carlos, and Paul will probably experience what Sarah Vowell's mom experienced, what the couple I interviewed at the beginning of this program experienced when they moved away from their small towns, which is, they find they don't exactly fit into the new worlds they move to, but they no longer fit in their hometown anymore, either. As Letta Sneed, the wife of the couple at the beginning of the show said--
<v Ira Glass>如果他们的楼房实际上是一种小镇，那么当他们搬走时，萨南托尼奥、卡洛斯和保罗可能会经历莎拉·沃威尔的妈妈经历过的事，我在本节目开头采访的那对夫妇搬离家乡时经历过的事，那就是，他们发现自己无法完全融入搬去的新世界，但他们也不再适合待在原来的家乡了。正如节目开头那对夫妇的妻子莱塔·斯尼德所说——

00:56:45.570 --> 00:57:08.400
<v Letta Sneed>So I do feel uncomfortable with living the city life, but on the other hand it's very hard for me to conceptualize going back to a small town. And I've often wondered, I often question myself, where do I fit? And I think for the past eight years, the sad truth is, that I feel in a way, a bit homeless, like I don't fit in either world.
<v Letta Sneed>所以我确实对过城市生活感到不舒服，但另一方面，让我构想回到小镇也很困难。我经常想知道，我经常质疑自己，我适合哪里？我想在过去的八年里，悲哀的事实是，我觉得某种程度上，有点无家可归，就像我不适合任何一个世界。

00:57:08.400 --> 00:57:10.560
<v Ira Glass>It's like you ate from the Tree of Knowledge.
<v Ira Glass>就像你吃了知识树的果子。

00:57:10.560 --> 00:57:23.590
<v Letta Sneed>Exactly.
<v Letta Sneed>完全正确。

00:57:23.590 --> 00:57:35.160
<v Ira Glass>Well, our program was produced today Alix Spiegel and myself with Nancy Updike, Julie Snyder, and Paul Tough. Contributing editor Sarah Vowell, Jack Hitt, and Margie Rochlin. Production help from Christina Stephens.
<v Ira Glass>好的，我们的节目今天由阿利克斯·斯皮格尔和我本人，以及南希·厄普代克、朱莉·斯奈德和保罗·塔夫制作。特约编辑莎拉·沃威尔、杰克·希特和玛吉·罗奇林。克里斯蒂娜·斯蒂芬斯提供了制作帮助。

00:57:35.160 --> 00:58:15.040
<v Ira Glass>[ACKNOWLEDGMENTS]
<v Ira Glass>[致谢]

00:58:15.040 --> 00:58:23.510
<v Ira Glass>[FUNDING CREDITS]
<v Ira Glass>[资助名单]

00:58:23.510 --> 00:58:29.710
<v Ira Glass>WBEZ management oversight by Torey Malatia, who could be heard most days wandering around the office singing this song.
<v Ira Glass>WBEZ管理监督托雷·马拉蒂亚，人们大部分时间都能听到他在办公室里徘徊唱着这首歌。

00:58:29.710 --> 00:58:34.020
<v Sarah Vowell>I will be a helper at home, at church, at school.
<v Sarah Vowell>我要做个好帮手，在家里、在教堂、在学校。

00:58:34.020 --> 00:58:39.020
<v Ira Glass>I'm Ira Glass, back next week with more stories of This American Life .
<v Ira Glass>我是艾拉·格拉斯，下周回来，带来更多《美国生活》的故事。
